From 2fdc4200fb357f0809cc99bf26692b65501fbe8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Eriksson <3308861+roer70@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 16:13:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] feat(machine): a machine file names its post, and the
 Setup page offers it

A .mch file may state controller.post, the name of a built-in post.
Machine.post carries it. post_offer now returns a PostOffer { post, why }:
the machine's named post when it is a registry post that serves the
mount and is not the setup's post, else the kind offer as before. The
Setup page's banner says which, and taking the offer queues
SelectPostNamed, so it rides undo. A mount never changes the post.

The reader refuses anything but a non-empty name; the validator also
refuses an unknown name and a post that does not serve the machine's
kind, at controller.post. 32 shipped machine files state their post
where the pairing is documented.

Fixes #2374

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
